OL,3,GNEWSARespecting pupil rights reduces
OL,4,Acrime, says mayor
OL,5,
OL,6,FA taxpayer-funded programme aiming to
OL,7,Fsupport children's rights is
OL,8,Fresponsible for London-wide reductions
OL,9,Fin persistent absenteeism, suspensions
OL,10,Fand exclusions, according to City Hall.
OL,12,FAt a visit to school in Kilburn, west
OL,13,FLondon on Monday, mayor Lord Khan said
OL,14,Fchildren who were excluded from school
OL,15,F"were twice as likely to get involved
OL,16,Fin violence".
OL,18,FBut Conservative London Assembly member
OL,19,FNeil Garratt questioned whether keeping
OL,20,Fpotentially disruptive pupils in
OL,21,Fschools would disrupt the education of
OL,22,Fothers.
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
